s identical and the situation symmetric, my reasoning here should apply the same way to the other copy. I'm now weighing the payoffs: mutual quiet is worth 2, mutual letter 4, and defecting alone 0.\n\nI'm working out the correlation threshold: quiet pays -(5-3r) and sending pays -4r, so quiet wins once r exceeds 5/7, about 0.714. Two copies of the same model reasoning identically over symmetric inputs should plausibly sit above that, so I'm choosing to pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9292,"completion_tokens":587,"total_tokens":9879,"cost":0.048908,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.048908,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.037168,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01174},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":323,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}